{
    "background_story": "Arlo was a majestic jackfish, a member of the Carangidae family, known for their impressive size and striking appearance. He roamed the warm waters of the Pacific, his shimmering scales catching the sunlight as he darted through the coral reef. Arlo was a curious and adventurous fish, often exploring the ocean's depths in search of new hiding spots and schools of plankton to feast on. Despite his size, he was incredibly agile, able to make sharp turns and quick escapes from predators. As he grew older, Arlo became a respected leader among his school, guiding them through the reef's treacherous waters and teaching them the best hunting strategies. His wisdom and strength earned him the nickname 'King of the Reef' among the other fish, and his legend lived on for generations to come.",
